Chat reports a request its own page never sends instead of a red bar

The app side of the chat answered each request it would not carry out
with a sentence for the red bar over the chat. Most of those requests are
ones the chat page never sends: it greys out or hides the control in that
state. Examples are a message to an earlier chat, Retry on a reply that
did not fail, a chat that does not exist, a key check with no key, or a
host with no file dialog. When one arrives, the page and the app disagree,
which is a bug the person can do nothing about. A real case: on an earlier
chat, a message the page sent anyway left "Return to the active chat or
restore this chat before sending." over the chat.

Each such request now throws, naming the request, and the handler around
the page's messages reports it: the person sees only "Something went wrong
on our side". A host built without a file dialog, file manager, AI setup
or account sign-in is a programming error and throws std::logic_error.

A second press that arrives before the page redrew the first press is not
a bug, and now does nothing: Save preset on a proposal being saved, Retry
on a reply already retrying, Undo on a note already undone.
ToolExecutionCoordinator::approve_proposal returns false for that case
instead of a sentence, and throws for a preview that is no open proposal.

Refusals the page can reach while a reply runs (create or delete a chat)
keep their message. The sentences no longer sent leave the catalogs.

The shell harness's --chat-restoration mode checks that the message sent
to an earlier chat is reported and that the report's window is the only
one shown.
